#==============================================================================================
#
#   typed_array - JS::Uint8Array before luce-js: a cell viewing an ArrayBuffer
#
#   DESCRIPTION:
#       Port of Libraries/LibJS/Runtime/TypedArray.cpp (lines 23-120, 475-760) and TypedArray.h
#       for Uint8Array, as the stand-in of DESIGN.md §3.6 that byte streams need (region p2s):
#       `Uint8Array::create`, `Construct(%Uint8Array%, « buffer, byteOffset, length »)` (the
#       constructor's InitializeTypedArrayFromArrayBuffer path), `typed_array_from`, the witness
#       record operations and `data()`. Its buffers are fixed-length, so [[ArrayLength]] and
#       [[ByteLength]] are never auto. The other kinds, element access and the prototypes are
#       phase 3.
